# Documented escape hatch for Trivy image scanning.
#
# The CI gate fails the build on any HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability in the whole
# image (application dependencies + base). Chainguard is continuously rebuilt to
# carry ~zero known CVEs, so this should stay (nearly) empty. Every entry below
# is a knowingly accepted, dated risk — re-check and remove when upstream ships
# a fix.

# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools path traversal (fixed upstream in 78.1.1).
# Present only as setuptools 70.3.0 in the Chainguard BASE image's system Python
# (Trivy target "Python", /usr/lib/.../site-packages) — NOT in our application
# venv, which ships setuptools 84.2.1. setuptools is build-time tooling and is
# not invoked by the running service. It cannot be removed from the distroless
# runtime (no shell for `RUN rm`); it clears when Chainguard rebuilds its base.
# Accepted: 2026-11-09 · re-check: 2026-12-09
CVE-2025-47273
